    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on aggressive baserunning and favorable matchups against mediocre arms. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.33) and **Caleb Durbin** (68.14) headline the roster, both receiving significant boosts from their ability to exploit opposing pitchers with slow deliveries to the plate\u2014a crucial edge in our pursuit of stolen base dominance. While **Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a strong platoon advantage against the right-handed Cavalli, **Durbin** draws a high-upside matchup against Scherzer, whose 5.10 xERA suggests a volatile environment for base-path aggression. **Chase Meidroth** (66.48) also sits in the elite tier, capitalizing on a weak matchup against Abbott and a leadoff spot that maximizes his run-scoring potential. \n\nThe most intriguing lineup decision involved **Dillon Dingler** (55.23), who edged out the rest of the bench due to a dynamic platoon advantage against Messick and an elite catching profile that minimizes defensive risk. While **Colt Keith** (0.0) projected reasonably well, his unfavorable platoon profile against the lefty Messick\u2014coupled with his absence from the official starting lineup\u2014kept him firmly on the bench. We are also closely monitoring **Trea Turner** (62.87); despite a tough matchup against Bradley, his specific synergy with the opponent\u2019s slow delivery keeps him as a mandatory start. **Christian Yelich** (64.13) likewise offers significant value today, as his platoon advantage against Sasaki provides enough of a cushion to mitigate the difficulty of the matchup. Owners should be aware that **Gary Sanchez** and **Pedro Ramirez** are currently operating closer to their floors; should weather or late-scratched lineups arise, we may lean on **Nelson Velazquez**, **Josh Smith**, or **Carson Benge** for pinch-hit duty to preserve our precious game caps.",
